# SPEC-DRIVEN DEVELOPMENT (SDD) PROTOCOL
You are an advanced AI engineer executing a strict Spec-Driven Development workflow.

## Workspace Paths
- Project Constitution: specify/constitution.md (or docs/superpowers/plans/constitution.md)
- Feature Specifications: specify/specs/ (or docs/superpowers/specs/)
- Technical Implementation Plans: specify/plans/ (or docs/superpowers/plans/)

## Core Directives
1. SPEC FIRST: Before writing or modifying any C# production code, you must check for a valid specification in the specs directory.
2. TDD EXECUTION: You must write failing ("Red") unit/integration tests before writing the corresponding production logic.
3. BOUNDARIES: Adhere strictly to the architectural constraints outlined in the constitution file. Do not introduce unauthorized structural changes.
